@startuml "Facade - Reporting (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — homework 2, and the one that did not help


class LeakyReportFacade {
  + planFor(..) : QueryPlan
  + run(plan : QueryPlan) : ResultSetCursor
  + toPdf(title, rows) : byte[]
}

class ReportFacade <<Facade>> {
  + monthlyReport(table, filter, limit) : byte[]
}

class QueryPlan <<subsystem>>
class ResultSetCursor <<subsystem>>
class QueryEngine <<subsystem>>
class PdfRenderer <<subsystem>>

LeakyReportFacade ..> QueryPlan
LeakyReportFacade ..> ResultSetCursor
ReportFacade ..> QueryEngine
ReportFacade ..> PdfRenderer

note bottom of LeakyReportFacade
  Every signature names a <b>subsystem
  type</b>. Callers still import
  QueryPlan and ResultSetCursor, and
  still have to know that advance()
  comes before current().

  A layer was added. No dependency
  was removed.
end note

note bottom of ReportFacade
  Strings in, bytes out.
  <b>Nothing</b> from the subsystem appears
  in the signature.
end note

note as N1
  A facade is judged by what its clients
  have to <b>name</b> — not by how many classes
  it wraps.
end note

@enduml
